{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013sWK1vdhYiZ36PCB4jKUTE","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the answer in the email discussions around the KIP-1270 decision.\\\\n\\\\n**The final agreed-upon name of the boolean config is: `processing.exception.handler.global.enabled`**\\\\n\\\\nThis name was suggested by Lucas Brutschy on **2026-02-20** at 09:41:00Z in his feedback on the KIP. He specifically recommended:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"How about processing.exception.handler.global.enabled instead of default.processing.exception.handler.invoke.for.global.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nArpit Goyal accepted this suggestion and confirmed on 2026-02-20 at 10:21:56Z that he had \\\\\\\"addressed all the points mentioned above and updated the KIP.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThis config was introduced as a deprecated boolean flag to safely extend the ProcessingExceptionHandler mechanism to GlobalKTable processing errors, allowing users to opt-in to the feature in Kafka Streams 4.3, with the expectation that it would become the default behavior (non-configurable) in Kafka Streams 5.0.\\\\n\\\\n**Source files:**\\\\n- `/store/events/2026/02/20/mail-59c5fd3092adaf090832eeba-08518722.md` (Lucas Brutschy's suggestion)\\\\n- `/store/events/2026/02/20/mail-d0ea5a94789da80c21eb21d1-6f0bfda8.md` (Arpit Goyal's acceptance)\\\\n- `/store/events/2026/02/22/mail-29c82027835a2e9497c104ed-e7a8ec27.md` (Matthias J. Sax confirming the config)\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"INDEX.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/02/20/mail-59c5fd3092adaf090832eeba-08518722.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/02/20/mail-d0ea5a94789da80c21eb21d1-6f0bfda8.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/02/21/github-api-apache-kafka-pr-21535-opened-dbeae35a.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/02/22/mail-29c82027835a2e9497c104ed-e7a8ec27.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":22.78,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":3,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":101530,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":35811,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.08970500000000001,\\\"input_tokens\\\":50,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1576}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c39e4e20-aef2-448e-bf47-4fcfe40d4e98","uuid":"63aaaf6a-48d0-4659-b406-1ffa6b68164f","timestamp":"2026-09-27T18:28:51.166Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the answer in the email discussions around the KIP-1270 decision.\\\\n\\\\n**The final agreed-upon name of the boolean config is: `processing.exception.handler.global.enabled`**\\\\n\\\\nThis name was suggested by Lucas Brutschy on **2026-02-20** at 09:41:00Z in his feedback on the KIP. He specifically recommended:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"How about processing.exception.handler.global.enabled instead of default.processing.exception.handler.invoke.for.global.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nArpit Goyal accepted this suggestion and confirmed on 2026-02-20 at 10:21:56Z that he had \\\\\\\"addressed all the points mentioned above and updated the KIP.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThis config was introduced as a deprecated boolean flag to safely extend the ProcessingExceptionHandler mechanism to GlobalKTable processing errors, allowing users to opt-in to the feature in Kafka Streams 4.3, with the expectation that it would become the default behavior (non-configurable) in Kafka Streams 5.0.\\\\n\\\\n**Source files:**\\\\n- `/store/events/2026/02/20/mail-59c5fd3092adaf090832eeba-08518722.md` (Lucas Brutschy's suggestion)\\\\n- `/store/events/2026/02/20/mail-d0ea5a94789da80c21eb21d1-6f0bfda8.md` (Arpit Goyal's acceptance)\\\\n- `/store/events/2026/02/22/mail-29c82027835a2e9497c104ed-e7a8ec27.md` (Matthias J. Sax confirming the config)\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"INDEX.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/02/20/mail-59c5fd3092adaf090832eeba-08518722.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/02/20/mail-d0ea5a94789da80c21eb21d1-6f0bfda8.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/02/21/github-api-apache-kafka-pr-21535-opened-dbeae35a.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/02/22/mail-29c82027835a2e9497c104ed-e7a8ec27.md\\\"],\\\"seconds\\\":22.78,\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"turns\\\":3,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"cache_read_tokens\\\":101530,\\\"cache_write_tokens\\\":35811,\\\"cost_usd\\\":0.08970500000000001,\\\"input_tokens\\\":50,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1576}}\"}","_meta":{"fastmcp":{"wrap_result":true}},"structuredContent":{"result":"{\"answer\":\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I found the answer in the email discussions around the KIP-1270 decision.\\n\\n**The final agreed-upon name of the boolean config is: `processing.exception.handler.global.enabled`**\\n\\nThis name was suggested by Lucas Brutschy on **2026-02-20** at 09:41:00Z in his feedback on the KIP. He specifically recommended:\\n\\n> \\\"How about processing.exception.handler.global.enabled instead of default.processing.exception.handler.invoke.for.global.\\\"\\n\\nArpit Goyal accepted this suggestion and confirmed on 2026-02-20 at 10:21:56Z that he had \\\"addressed all the points mentioned above and updated the KIP.\\\"\\n\\nThis config was introduced as a deprecated boolean flag to safely extend the ProcessingExceptionHandler mechanism to GlobalKTable processing errors, allowing users to opt-in to the feature in Kafka Streams 4.3, with the expectation that it would become the default behavior (non-configurable) in Kafka Streams 5.0.\\n\\n**Source files:**\\n- `/store/events/2026/02/20/mail-59c5fd3092adaf090832eeba-08518722.md` (Lucas Brutschy's suggestion)\\n- `/store/events/2026/02/20/mail-d0ea5a94789da80c21eb21d1-6f0bfda8.md` (Arpit Goyal's acceptance)\\n- `/store/events/2026/02/22/mail-29c82027835a2e9497c104ed-e7a8ec27.md` (Matthias J. Sax confirming the config)\",\"error\":null,\"files\":[\"INDEX.md\",\"events/2026/02/20/mail-59c5fd3092adaf090832eeba-08518722.md\",\"events/2026/02/20/mail-d0ea5a94789da80c21eb21d1-6f0bfda8.md\",\"events/2026/02/21/github-api-apache-kafka-pr-21535-opened-dbeae35a.md\",\"events/2026/02/22/mail-29c82027835a2e9497c104ed-e7a8ec27.md\"],